{"id": "EUVD-2026-97009", "enisaUuid": "329d2edb-a7d6-3403-8998-99d475ad9e3a", "description": "Predibase LoRAX through 0.12.1 contains a sensitive information exposure vulnerability that writes the caller-supplied api_token from POST /generate request bodies into router logs. Attackers with access to router logs or OTLP trace backends can recover other users' private-adapter tokens recorded through the instrumented GenerateParameters span field.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:26:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:41:34", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/predibase-lorax-generate-api-token-logging", "https://github.com/predibase/lorax/blob/c0e5798318a6b826572c612ddd4cf44621aa4add/router/src/server.rs#L584-L596", "https://github.com/predibase/lorax/blob/c0e5798318a6b826572c612ddd4cf44621aa4add/router/src/lib.rs#L182-L188", "https://github.com/predibase/lorax", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/predibase-lorax-through-0.12.1-api-token-exposure-via-router-logs"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mqw3-26gg-6g3w", "CVE-2026-108858"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "740c8706-e85b-39f5-84a3-2bdda83675d2", "product": {"name": "LoRAX", "vendor": {"name": "Predibase"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.12.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ae21882d-2db8-3d90-8a87-2ca9fb7fb74f", "vendor": {"name": "Predibase"}}], "isExploited": false}